# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite portfolio project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **File**: `package.json`, `package-lock.json`
- **Action**: Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- **Version**: Added to dependencies (178 packages installed)

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **File**: `src/App.tsx`
- **Action**: Added Vercel Analytics component to the application
- **Changes**:
  - Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component to both mobile and desktop render paths
  - Placed the Analytics component at the top level of the app structure to ensure tracking on all pages

### Implementation Details
Following the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects, the Analytics component was added as a direct child of the root `<div className="app">` element. This ensures:
- Analytics tracking works on both mobile (Fallback2D only) and desktop (Unity + Fallback2D) views
- Minimal intrusion to existing code structure
- Proper data collection across all user interactions

## Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ **Build Test**: Successfully ran `npm run build` - project compiles without errors
2. ✅ **Linting**: Ran `npm run lint` - App.tsx has no linting errors (pre-existing errors in other files remain unchanged)
3. ✅ **Git Staging**: All modified files properly staged:
   - package.json (dependency added)
   - package-lock.json (lock file updated)
   - src/App.tsx (Analytics component integrated)

## Next Steps for Deployment

To complete the setup and start collecting analytics:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel (via `vercel deploy` or Git integration)
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project dashboard
   - Select "Analytics" in the sidebar
   - Click the "Enable" button
3. After deployment, verify analytics collection by checking the browser Network tab for analytics requests
4. View collected data in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section

## Technical Notes
- The implementation follows React/Vite-specific instructions from the official documentation
- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact application performance
- No additional configuration files needed - the component works out of the box
- Analytics data will only be collected once the feature is enabled in the Vercel dashboard
